Below is a single search-and-replace patch that makes “{…}” argument groups recurse into the LaTeX grammar (so that commands, formulas, etc. inside braces will be highlighted) rather than treating them as plain strings. We replace the one “string”-variant that covered both “[…]” and “{…}” by two modes: one for square-bracket options (still a string) and one for curly braces (a recursive “subst” mode containing COMMAND).

```javascript
### src/languages/latex.js
<<<<<<< SEARCH
            {
              className: 'string', // because it looks like attributes in HTML tags
              variants: [
                {begin: /\[/, end: /\]/},
                {begin: /\{/, end: /\}/}
              ]
            },
=======
            {
              className: 'string', // options in [ … ]
              begin: /\[/, end: /\]/,
            },
            {
              className: 'subst',    // recurse into { … }
              begin: /\{/, end: /\}/,
              contains: [ COMMAND ]
            },
>>>>>>> REPLACE
```

With this change, anything inside `{ … }` will re-invoke the normal LaTeX modes (so backslash-commands, math, etc. are highlighted) instead of being lumped into a single string.
